      "username": "EvanDan55",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/evandan55/{size}/2374_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-03-17T18:11:38.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Ah, I see, so it's a chance to use the card you draw at the end. Makes sense. At first I just saw it as a way to get an additional power since you sacrifice a play on it. But it's not like O-X is very short of playing cards, with both Electro-Deployment Units. I guess Slip Through Time's function is kinda niche, but it can be nice bait for ongoing sacrifices. I need to play him more--I want to drop a Self-Sabotage, Singularity, and Reset combo. That sounds like a ton of fun.</p><p>I haven't utilized his other powers, though. I usually focus on playing all of his components.</p>",
